Shedding a little more light...  If you look at the code (I happen to
have the printout right in front of me, as I'm working on the Scroll Effects
section of the Spoilers right now), the very first thing that the
enchant armor code does is pick a random piece of armor you're wearing.

This happens even before the code checks to see if you're confused,
if the scroll's cursed, etc.  So *definitely* make sure that you take
off *everything* except the piece of armor you want erode-proofed.

Also, it helps to engrave Elbereth or drop a scroll of scare monster
when enchanting armor like this.  That way you don't have to worry as
much about monsters sneaking up on you while you're butt-nekked.  <GRIN>

